<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olof Trätälja</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Olof the Tree-Feller, Olof Tretelgja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olof Trätälja, 'the Tree-Feller', is a legendary Swedish king of the Yngling line known from Ynglingatal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ynglinga-saga">Ynglinga saga</a>. Driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, he is said to have cleared the forests of Värmland and founded a settlement there, before being sacrificed to Odin by his people during a famine. The sagas make him the ancestor of the kings of Vestfold and so of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olof-tratalja.jpg" alt="Olof Trätälja" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerhard Munthe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ynglingesaga_24_Gerhard_Munthe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
